<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>The problem we're solving at Swimly</title>
</head>
<body style="font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, sans-serif; line-height: 1.6; color: #333; background-color: #f4f4f4; margin: 0; padding: 0;">
  <div style="max-width: 600px; margin: 20px auto; background: #fff; border-radius: 8px; overflow: hidden; box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);">

    <div style="background: #111827; padding: 40px 20px; text-align: center;">
      <h1 style="margin: 0; font-size: 28px; font-weight: 700; color: #00ff90;">Swimly</h1>
    </div>

    <div style="padding: 30px 20px;">
      <p style="font-size: 18px; margin-top: 0;">Hi {{#if name}}{{name}}{{else}}there{{/if}},</p>

      <p>I wanted to share a bit more about why we are building Swimly.</p>

      <p>Running a swim club in 2026 still means juggling spreadsheets for attendance, chasing parents on WhatsApp for payments, losing track of consent forms, and spending hours on admin that should take minutes. Every club we have spoken to tells us the same story.</p>

      <p>The tools that exist today were not built for swimming clubs. They are generic platforms that force you to bend your workflow around their limitations. Swim clubs have unique needs — squads, session registers, term-based billing, safeguarding compliance, parent communications — and they deserve a platform that understands that.</p>

      <p>That is exactly what Swimly is. Purpose-built for swim clubs, by people who understand how they actually work.</p>

      <div style="background: #F0FDF4; border-left: 4px solid #00ff90; padding: 20px; margin: 25px 0; border-radius: 4px;">
        <p style="margin: 0; color: #166534; font-weight: 600;">I have a question for you:</p>
        <p style="margin: 8px 0 0 0; color: #166534;">What is the biggest admin headache at your club right now? I would love to hear about it — just hit reply.</p>
      </div>

      <p>Your answer will directly shape what we build first.</p>

      <p style="margin-top: 30px;">
        Cheers,<br>
        <strong>Mike</strong><br>
        <span style="color: #64748B;">Founder of Swimly</span>
      </p>
    </div>

    <div style="background: #F8FAFC; padding: 20px; text-align: center; color: #64748B; font-size: 13px;">
      <p style="margin: 5px 0;">&copy; {{year}} Swimly. All rights reserved.</p>
      <p style="margin: 5px 0;"><a href="{{unsubscribeUrl}}" style="color: #64748B; text-decoration: underline;">Unsubscribe</a></p>
    </div>

  </div>
</body>
</html>
